>> title: Collard Greens
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: greens, southern, pork, stew, side
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: greens, collards, turnip greens, mustard greens, mixed greens, pot likker, potlikker
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 40 min
>> slack: forgiving — salt goes in at the very end, because the pork is already salty and salt cannot come back out of the pot
>> pairs-with: ham-hock-stock, skillet-cornbread, hot-water-cornbread, black-eyed-peas

>> step: trim the ribs out, wash in three waters
Trim @collard greens{4%lb}(1.8 kg; thick ribs pulled out, leaves cut in wide ribbons) and wash them in three changes of water until no grit settles.

>> step: render 8 min
Render @thick-cut bacon{6%slices}(chopped) in a #Dutch oven{} for ~render{8%min}.

>> step: sweat 6 min
Sweat @&(~1)bacon{} with @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @garlic{4%cloves}(sliced) for ~sweat{6%min}.

>> step: stew covered 2 hr
Stew @&(~1)pork base{}, @&(~3)washed greens{} with @ham hock stock{3%qt}(2.8 L), @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, @light brown sugar{1%tsp}, @crushed red pepper{1/2%tsp} covered at a ~stew{2%hr}.

>> step: season at the very end
Season @&(~1)greens{} with @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @hot sauce{1%Tbs}.

Pour the liquid left in the pot into a cup and send it out beside the greens. That is pot likker.
